text:
I just got a LLM to write a user script that blocks pass key requests:<p><pre><code>    (() =&gt; {
      &#x2F;&#x2F; Sites check `window.PublicKeyCredential` to decide whether to offer passkeys.
      try { delete window.PublicKeyCredential; } catch (e) {}

      &#x2F;&#x2F; Block passkey requests from sites that skip the check. Password&#x2F;federated credentials still work.
      const creds = navigator.credentials;
      if (!creds) return;
      const refuse = () =&gt; Promise.reject(new DOMException(&quot;Passkeys are disabled.&quot;, &quot;NotAllowedError&quot;));
      const origGet = creds.get.bind(creds);
      const origCreate = creds.create.bind(creds);
      creds.get = (opts) =&gt; (opts &amp;&amp; opts.publicKey ? refuse() : origGet(opts));
      creds.create = (opts) =&gt; (opts &amp;&amp; opts.publicKey ? refuse() : origCreate(opts));
    })();</code></pre>
